# Construction App

## Backend setup

The Django API lives in `backend/` and uses PostgreSQL in every environment.
Configuration is read from `backend/.env`; copy `backend/.env.example` to that
path and set values appropriate to your machine. Do not commit `.env` or use the
example credentials in production.

Copy the example environment file and change its sample secret/password:

```bash
cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
```

Start the local PostgreSQL service (Docker Compose) and the API:

```bash
docker compose --env-file backend/.env up -d db
cd backend
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py createsuperuser
python manage.py runserver
```

The API is served at `http://127.0.0.1:8000`. JWT tokens are available at
`/api/auth/token/` and `/api/auth/token/refresh/`. Set `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` to
the frontend's exact origin(s); the example includes common local React ports.
The database uses a persistent Compose volume. On Hermes, set the PostgreSQL
host and allowed hosts in its untracked `backend/.env` file and use either this
Compose service or a native PostgreSQL instance with the same environment keys.
